## 4. Comprehensive Mitigation Checklist

| Category | Recommendation | Code Example |
|----------|----------------|--------------|
| **A. Harden HTTP Headers** | Use `helmet` middleware to set common security headers. | ```js\nconst helmet = require('helmet');\napp.use(helmet());\n``` |
| **b. Turn on HSTS** | Force browsers to use HTTPS and block downgrade attacks. | ```js\napp.use(helmet.hsts({maxAge: 31536000, includeSubDomains: true}));\n``` |
| **c. Content Security Policy (CSP)** | Mitigate XSS by specifying allowed sources. | ```js\napp.use(\n  helmet.contentSecurityPolicy({\n    directives: {\n      defaultSrc: ['\'self\''],\n      scriptSrc: ['\'self\''],\n      styleSrc: ['\'self\''],\n      imgSrc: ['\'self\''],\n    },\n  })\n);\n``` |
| **d. No Sniff** | Prevent browsers from MIME‑sniffing. | Already covered by `helmet.xssFilter()` or part of `helmet()` (but you can add explicit). |
| **e. Redirect HTTP → HTTPS** | If behind a reverse proxy, add `app.enable('trust proxy')` followed by a middleware that rejects non‑HTTPS requests. | ```js\napp.enable('trust proxy');\napp.use((req, res, next) => {\n  if (req.secure) next();\n  else res.redirect(301, 'https://' + req.headers.host + req.url);\n});\n``` |
