```

```js
const helmet = require('helmet');
app.use(helmet());           // Automatically sets many secure headers
app.use(helmet.contentSecurityPolicy({
  directives: {
    defaultSrc: ["'self'"],
    scriptSrc: ["'self'"]
  }
}));
```

> *Helps mitigate XSS, clickjacking, MIME‑type sniffing, etc.*

### 3.2  Limit Cross‑Origin Requests (`cors`)

```bash
npm install cors
```

```js
const cors = require('cors');
app.use(cors({
  origin: 'https://my-frontend.example.com',   // Restrict to known domains
  methods: ['GET'],                            // Allowed methods
  credentials: false
}));
```

> *Reduces data leakage via unintended cross‑origin fetches.*

### 3.3  Rate Limiting (`express-rate-limit`)

```bash
npm install express-rate-limit
```

```js
const rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');
const limiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 60 * 1000,   // 1 minute
  max: 60,               // limit each IP to 60 requests per windowMs
  handler: (req, res) => {
    res.status(429).json({ error: 'Too many requests, please try again later.'});
  }
});
app.use(limiter); // Apply to all requests
```

> *Defends against brute‑force and denial‑of‑service attempts.*

### 3.4  CSRF Protection (if you add POST routes in future)

```bash
